WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.536
Where you can fine-tune today.

2
00:00:01.816 --> 00:00:11.288
Hosted fine-tuning has changed quickly, so treat this as a snapshot checked on the review date, and check each provider’s current docs before you plan around it.

3
00:00:11.568 --> 00:00:12.613
OpenAI.

4
00:00:12.893 --> 00:00:17.032
Supervised fine-tuning (and preference tuning) on GPT-4.

5
00:00:17.312 --> 00:00:22.859
1 snapshots is documented, but OpenAI is winding the self-serve platform down.

6
00:00:23.139 --> 00:00:41.592
Its deprecations page says that from May 2026 organizations that had never fine-tuned can’t start, that active existing customers can create jobs until January 6, 2027, and that fine-tuned models keep serving until their base model is deprecated.

7
00:00:41.872 --> 00:00:42.640
Google.

8
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:50.472
The Gemini API and AI Studio currently have no model that supports fine-tuning, according to Google’s own page.

9
00:00:50.752 --> 00:00:55.211
Supervised tuning for several Gemini models (including Gemini 2.

10
00:00:55.491 --> 00:00:56.515
5 and 3.

11
00:00:56.795 --> 00:01:07.483
x Flash variants) is offered on Google Cloud, in the platform documented under the Vertex AI docs path and now titled Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform.

12
00:01:07.763 --> 00:01:09.000
Amazon Bedrock.

13
00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.315
Fine-tuning is offered for Amazon’s Nova models and several Meta Llama models.

14
00:01:14.595 --> 00:01:15.363
Claude.

15
00:01:15.643 --> 00:01:21.595
We found no fine-tuning option for current Claude models in Anthropic’s API documentation.

16
00:01:21.875 --> 00:01:29.640
Anthropic’s own fine-tuning material covers one model: Claude 3 Haiku on Amazon Bedrock, in one US Region.

17
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:44.405
That model is now retired (on the Claude API since April 2026 and in that Bedrock Region since September 2026), and Bedrock accepts no new fine-tuning jobs on a model once it is Legacy.

18
00:01:44.685 --> 00:01:52.749
Bedrock’s supported-models table still lists the Claude 3 Haiku row, which is a good reminder to check the lifecycle page as well.

19
00:01:53.029 --> 00:02:01.733
In practice: you can’t fine-tune a current Claude model, so with Claude you steer behavior with prompts, examples, structured outputs, and retrieval.

20
00:02:02.013 --> 00:02:02.803
Mistral.

21
00:02:03.083 --> 00:02:08.480
Its fine-tuning page marks the feature as deprecated and no longer actively supported.

22
00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.235
The pattern matters more than any single row.

23
00:02:11.515 --> 00:02:25.040
Hosted fine-tuning of closed models is shrinking, while open-weight models (week 1) can be fine-tuned by anyone with a GPU and a library such as Hugging Face TRL, and the result is yours to keep.

24
00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:28.861
That is why this studio trains open models with LoRA next week.

25
00:02:29.141 --> 00:02:36.373
It is also a model-selection lesson: a feature that depends on a hosted fine-tune depends on that provider’s roadmap.
